      "why": "iterative is the smallest-area family (single shared datapath, no per-stage registers). It is the only family I can plausibly use to minimise area. The throughput constraint (>=32 Msps) and the 0.5us p99-batch constraint are the hard gates: with 1 result/cycle, Fmax must be >=32 MHz and the 32-deep burst must drain in <=0.5us. I keep data_width/n_iter in the band that can reach accuracy_bits >=12 (max_abs_err <= 2^-12) while staying small; angle_guard/frac_guard are left to the search to trade a little accuracy headroom against area. This is the area-minimising corner the selection rule (min area) will ultimately pick, so it must be well-mapped."
